\ Ten authoritative sum-preserving Pastafarian Calendar vectors.
\ Only the AC.1 canonical table is used; the historical mutant
\ table is explicitly excluded. These are expensive integration
\ tests, so they are never part of the default 72-group quick suite.
\ Each vector resets the full calculation and checks the five
\ canonical numeric indices. No results are preloaded into the
\ real date calculation routine.
\ Native CAL has not compiled or executed these checks.

To check canonical date vector one:
  Calculate a complete date for -15055671 and -15055671.
  If the complete date status is not 1,
    put "Canonical date vector 1 failed to calculate." into the check report; exit.
  If the complete date answer's year number is not 5000,
    put "Canonical date vector 1 has the wrong year." into the check report; exit.
  If the complete date answer's cutlet name index is not 10,
    put "Canonical date vector 1 has the wrong cutlet." into the check report; exit.
  If the complete date answer's cutlet day is not 503,
    put "Canonical date vector 1 has the wrong cutlet day." into the check report; exit.
  If the complete date answer's month name index is not 20,
    put "Canonical date vector 1 has the wrong month." into the check report; exit.
  If the complete date answer's month day is not 56,
    put "Canonical date vector 1 has the wrong month day." into the check report; exit.

